## 5. EcoSuit assignment

Keep Layer 0–2 of the exo (springs, SEAs, cable-SEAs) for gait and tools. Give V-EBMs the jobs that are short-stroke, high-speed, vacuum-side, and allowed to be binary.

| Use | Why it fits | Why it is not a stretch |
|---|---|---|
| Plate segment latches | 4 N pulls a pin or closes a scale; 1 mm is a latch stroke; stack for redundancy | Armor that opens is the Iron Man read |
| Helmet visor / slit cover | Fast, light, no lubricant | kV packaging in the helmet ring |
| Rear-hatch secondary catch | Vacuum-side only | Must inhibit in the airlock |
| Dust cover / sensor door | High bandwidth, low mass | Dust-tolerant cover over the cell itself |
| External tool-release / sample-bag deploy | Gripper already shown | Not finger flexion inside the bladder |
| Antenna / cover deploy | Classic spacecraft mechanism replacement | Already the paper’s intended market |

**Do not use in MK.I as:**
- Hip, knee, or elbow primary drive
- Anything inside the bladder / cabin
- Uninhibited operation during airlock cycle

